  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HIV&amp;AIDS, Gender and Poverty Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Goal: Families and communities in the Diocese of Mariannhill, through the church are able to respond to challenges associated with HIV &amp;AIDS and poverty.
Outcomes: 
1. At least 44 capacitated Parish AIDS co-ordinators and 460 new HIV&amp;AIDS volunteers implementing HIV &amp;AIDS programmes, providing psycho-social support in their Parishes.  
2. Increased awareness and information dissemination around HIV&amp;AIDS within sodalities in the Diocese of Mariannhill.
3. Strengthened Capacity and support to local parish/mission in project management in responding to HIV&amp;AIDS challenges.  
4. Children in the Diocese of Mariannhill responding to challenges related to HIV&amp;AIDS and demanding and protecting their rights.

At least 44 Parish Coordinators, 500 volunteers and 15,000 families in the Mariannhill Diocese are set to benefit from a proposed programme being implemented by Home and Family Life Foundation (HFLF) in KwaZulu Natal, South Africa. This will be done through the capacity development and strengthening of volunteers, Church structures, children and stakeholders within the Diocese. Additionally, the programme will spearhead issues around awareness raising, information dissemination as a precursor to mobilisation, campaign work and advocacy. This will be achieved through support to local parish/missions. Finally, the programme also seeks to empower children especially Orphans and other vulnerable Children (OVC) in rights consciousness to enable children to claim and protect their rights. This action will be executed initially over 3 years with the hope that CAFOD will agree to extend the programme support to 5 years for effective programming and allow for measuring impact.</narrative>
  </description>
